  "source": "The incumbent measurement of control-v4, the first manifest whose trajectory is computed in simulated time. The protocol is control-v3's, constant for constant, with its wall-clock pacing and its solve deadline removed; the recipe, both fits and the calibration are unchanged, and the generic artifact is the same fingerprint 9f7e7b17 control-v3's own incumbent run produced. Every score below reproduces control-v3's reference to every printed digit, because the unloaded runs that measured it applied every solved command anyway. What changed is that this one still does when the host is busy: it was made while four concurrent synthetic-tier runs and the fast test suite loaded the machine, and the run made immediately after it under the same load produced byte-identical tracking arrays on all four trials while its recorded solve times differed. A later run's generic position or attitude RMSE may not exceed these values by more than this manifest's reference allowance, and the rule gates only a trial and metric the generic arm already met it on. It met it on none of them.",
